==Usage==
Memory erasure spells are the only type of magic allowed to be used on the body. They are not qualified as forbidden magic, and are mostly used by the Knights Moralis. It is highly likely that the Knights are the only people permitted to use  the spell, which they utilize wipe the memory of the witches they catch practicing [[Forbidden Magic|forbidden]] or illegal magic{{Ref|m|11}}, or who have commit serious crimes{{Ref|m|48}}.

When [[Qifrey]] was found by [[Beldaruit]], together with some [[Knights Moralis]], after having been a victim of the [[Brimmed Cap Group|Brimmed Caps]], it was quickly revealed that the Brimcaps had wiped his memory, having used this spell on him.{{Ref|m|36}} Unlike the more selective memory erasure practiced by the [[Pointed Hat Witches]], the instances where Qifrey casts memory erasure spells only rid their victims of the memory of a specific event. When the magic of the Knights is mentioned, it's to "wipe the memories of magic" and not a plain memory wipe, which might imply the magic has precision to a degree. 

How it works, however, is currently unknown. The boy had his mind entirely wiped, and lacked some basic knowledge as a result.<ref>In the comics Shirahama Kamome drew to celebrate character birthdays, he is shown not knowing what a birthday is.</ref>

Ironically, Qifrey has also used memory erasure spells himself, specifically on [[Olruggio]]. While it is implied he had done so several times prior, the spell we see him using was similar to the one Easthies uses in chapter 11, and hidden under the flap of his cap.{{Ref|m|40}} The variant Qifrey had used specifically wipes all memories within a specific time frame, going from an unspecified time before the spell was used to the moment it was activated. {{Cite}} Qifrey had also used a memory erasure spell on [[Mr. Nolnoa]] to avoid him contacting the authorities after discovering the properties of Iguin's ink pot.{{Ref|m|13}}

